# Plugin Adapter Map

Purpose:
  Map external plugin skills to SDDRA chain graph arms.
  Only general-purpose skills are adapted; domain-specific ones are excluded.

External Repo:
  D:\Tasks\ai_code\sddra.ai\tmp\external-repo-audit\repo-01
  Source: https://github.com/obra/superpowers

Accepted Skills:
  brainstorming -> P1 (prompt arm)
    Why: Refines rough ideas into design before implementation
    How: Used during prompt analysis phase
    Adaptation: Keep 3 paths (Spike/Bounded/Architectural), map to chain selection

  test-driven-development -> QA chain
    Why: Enforces RED-GREEN-REFACTOR cycle
    How: Used during test suite stage
    Adaptation: Map to TS stage in feature/bugfix chains

  systematic-debugging -> Bugfix/Hotfix chains
    Why: 4-phase root cause investigation
    How: Used during AR stage in bugfix chain
    Adaptation: Replace simple "Architecture" stage with root cause investigation

  writing-plans -> S1 (sdd arm)
    Why: Breaks work into bite-sized tasks
    How: Used during task creation
    Adaptation: Map to task generation phase

  using-git-worktrees -> C1 (code arm)
    Why: Isolated workspace per task
    How: Used during code implementation
    Adaptation: Use for project isolation before code generation

  requesting-code-review -> R1 (review arm)
    Why: Pre-review checklist
    How: Used during human review
    Adaptation: Map to review gate checklist

  receiving-code-review -> R1 (review arm)
    Why: Responding to feedback
    How: Used when human requests changes
    Adaptation: Map to revision workflow

  dispatching-parallel-agents -> Scheduler
    Why: Concurrent subagent workflows
    How: Used during task scheduling
    Adaptation: Map to parallel execution in chain graph

  writing-skills -> Skill creation
    Why: Methodology for creating new skills
    How: Used when creating new .sdd skills
    Adaptation: Use for skill authoring guidelines

  verification-before-completion -> R1 (review arm)
    Why: Ensure work is actually done
    How: Used before marking complete
    Adaptation: Map to verification criteria

Rejected Skills:
  executing-plans: superseded by SDDRA chain graph
  finishing-a-development-branch: project-specific
  subagent-driven-development: covered by chain graph
  using-superpowers: meta-skill, not needed
  condition-based-waiting: too specific
  defense-in-depth: covered by security rules
  root-cause-tracing: covered by systematic-debugging
  visual-companion: UI-specific, rejected
  spec-document-reviewer-prompt: domain-specific

Integration:
  Each adapted skill becomes a .sdd file under:
    .sdd/skills/plugin-adapters/{skill-name}.sdd

  Chain arms reference adapted skills in their skills section.


State: +

